  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Utah has $5.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $4B in obligations. Award activity shows 7,601 awards with an average award size of $665K. Obligations are down 3.2% year over year. Fiscal-year context shows a rise from $4B in FY21 to $7.2B in FY24, then a decline to $5.2B in FY25 and $5.1B in FY26. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $2.9B. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP is the largest vendor by obligations at $2.9B. Other notable buyers include the Department of the Treasury at $400M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $117M. Nondefense industry categories with sizable obligations include Nonferrous Metal Rolling at $373M and Engineering Services at $200M. This mix makes Utah a state with concentrated defense spending and a handful of large vendors and industries capturing a large share of obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Utah?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for $4B of Utah obligations, making defense spending highly concentrated. Utah has 7,601 awards with an average award size of $665K, which points to a mix of large prime awards and smaller contracts. Obligations are down 3.2% year over year, and the state total sits at $5.1B for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal obligations in Utah?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing leads industries with $2.9B in obligations. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP leads vendors with $2.9B in obligations, and ASAHI REFINING USA INC follows with $373M. Other top industries include Nonferrous Metal Rolling at $373M and Engineering Services at $200M."
      }
    ]
